1
00:02:15,530 --> 00:02:18,530
Hi, Mom.

2
00:02:18,530 --> 00:02:19,530
Hi, Robbie.

3
00:02:19,530 --> 00:02:20,530
You're home from school early.

4
00:02:20,530 --> 00:02:22,530
Yeah, they're getting the assembly hall

5
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:23,530
ready for the graduation ceremony,

6
00:02:23,530 --> 00:02:25,530
so we all got to go home early.

7
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:27,530
Too noisy to study.

8
00:02:27,530 --> 00:02:28,530
Well, now that you're here,

9
00:02:28,530 --> 00:02:29,530
you can help me with dinner.

10
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:32,530
I need those potatoes peeled and sliced.

11
00:02:32,530 --> 00:02:35,530
Mom, give me a break.

12
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:39,530
Alexandra's coming over to help me study for my math final Alexandra

13
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:41,530
Well, in that case,

14
00:02:41,530 --> 00:02:44,530
you can wash the dishes and clean up after dinner.

15
00:02:44,530 --> 00:02:48,530
Can I invite Alexandra to stay for dinner?

16
00:02:48,530 --> 00:02:49,530
Of course.

17
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:51,530
Thanks, Mom.

18
00:02:51,530 --> 00:02:56,530
You and Alexandra

19
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:58,530
have become good friends, haven't you?

20
00:02:58,530 --> 00:03:00,530
Yes. I like her.

21
00:03:00,530 --> 00:03:01,530
She's a terrific person.

22
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:05,530
I'm going to miss her

23
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:07,530
when she goes back to Greece.

24
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:12,530
Would you like to give her a little farewell party?

25
00:03:12,530 --> 00:03:14,530
Mom, that would be terrific!

26
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:17,530
Maybe we could make it a surprise.

27
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:19,530
Oh, I don't know.

28
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:21,530
Surprise parties don't always work out.

29
00:03:21,530 --> 00:03:24,530
Well, we could tell her

30
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:26,530
it's a graduation party for me.

31
00:03:26,530 --> 00:03:28,530
When Alexandra arrives,

32
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:30,530
we'll surprise her.

33
00:03:30,530 --> 00:03:32,530
Well, I suppose that might work.

34
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:36,530
I'd like to give her a nice going-away present.

35
00:03:36,530 --> 00:03:37,530
Fine.

36
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:39,530
There's only one problem.

37
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:41,530
What's that?

38
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:44,530
I'm broke.

39
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:46,530
I should have saved some money.

40
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:48,530
I'm sure Alexandra

41
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:50,530
would be happy with something simple, Robbie.

42
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:51,530
I know.

43
00:03:51,530 --> 00:03:52,530
But, well,

44
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:55,530
I'd like to give her something nice

45
00:03:55,530 --> 00:03:56,530
to remember me by.

46
00:03:56,530 --> 00:04:00,530
Maybe I could borrow some money from you and Dad.

47
00:04:00,530 --> 00:04:02,530
It's all right with me

48
00:04:02,530 --> 00:04:04,530
if it's all right with your dad.

49
00:04:04,530 --> 00:04:05,530
Thanks, Mom.

50
00:04:05,530 --> 00:04:06,530
I'll talk to him.

51
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:08,530
Is he still in his office?

52
00:04:08,530 --> 00:04:09,530
I think so.

53
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:11,530
Thanks, Mom.

54
00:04:11,530 --> 00:04:36,530
Robbie! Good luck! Robbie

55
00:04:36,530 --> 00:04:38,530
Here are the X-rays you wanted, Dr. Stewart.

56
00:04:38,530 --> 00:04:40,530
Oh. Thank you, Molly.

57
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:53,530
Now, let me check them.

58
00:04:53,530 --> 00:04:55,530
What do you think?

59
00:04:55,530 --> 00:04:58,530
I don't see any breaks or fractures.

60
00:04:58,530 --> 00:05:02,530
Well, well. Thank you, Molly.

61
00:05:02,530 --> 00:05:18,530
Thank you.

62
00:05:18,530 --> 00:05:19,530
Come in!

63
00:05:19,530 --> 00:05:22,530
Hi, Son.

64
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:25,530
Hi, Dad. Am I interrupting you?

65
00:05:25,530 --> 00:05:27,530
No, no, no, no.

66
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:28,530
What's up?

67
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:29,530
Can we talk?

68
00:05:29,530 --> 00:05:30,530
Sure.

69
00:05:30,530 --> 00:05:33,530
I need some help.

70
00:05:33,530 --> 00:05:36,530
Well, that's what fathers are for.

71
00:05:36,530 --> 00:05:38,530
Well, before I go to college,

72
00:05:38,530 --> 00:05:40,530
I have the whole summer ...

73
00:05:40,530 --> 00:05:41,530
Yes ...

74
00:05:41,530 --> 00:05:43,530
And I'm planning to get a job for the summer.

75
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:46,530
And what sort of job?

76
00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:49,530
I applied for a job as a lifeguard at the community pool.

77
00:05:49,530 --> 00:05:52,530
Sounds pretty good.

78
00:05:52,530 --> 00:05:55,530
Yes. I'll be earning pretty good money if I get it.

79
00:05:55,530 --> 00:05:58,530
But right now, I'm kind of short of cash.

80
00:05:58,530 --> 00:06:01,530
Who isn't?

81
00:06:01,530 --> 00:06:05,530
And my friend Alexandra is going back to Greece ...

82
00:06:05,530 --> 00:06:07,530
Nice girl.

83
00:06:07,530 --> 00:06:08,530
We'll all miss her.

84
00:06:08,530 --> 00:06:12,530
Mom says we can give her a going-away surprise party.

85
00:06:12,530 --> 00:06:13,530
Good idea.

86
00:06:13,530 --> 00:06:16,530
And I'd like to get her a nice gift ...

87
00:06:16,530 --> 00:06:18,530
What'd you have in mind?

88
00:06:18,530 --> 00:06:22,130
Well, a wristwatch,

89
00:06:22,130 --> 00:06:25,530
so she'll think of me when she looks at the time.

90
00:06:25,530 --> 00:06:27,530
Nothing flashy or expensive.

91
00:06:27,530 --> 00:06:30,530
Something simple--but a good one.

92
00:06:30,530 --> 00:06:33,530
Sounds fine, Robbie.

93
00:06:33,530 --> 00:06:35,530
Well, I saw a nice watch.

94
00:06:35,530 --> 00:06:37,530
But I'll need a loan.

95
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:39,530
If you could lend me the money,

96
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:42,530
I could pay you back out of my lifeguard salary.

97
00:06:42,530 --> 00:06:48,530
Well, I guess your mother and I can manage it.

98
00:06:48,530 --> 00:06:51,530
When do you need the money?

99
00:06:51,530 --> 00:06:53,530
Would tomorrow be OK?

100
00:06:53,530 --> 00:06:57,530
You've got it.

101
00:06:57,530 --> 00:06:59,530
Thanks, Dad.

102
00:06:59,530 --> 00:07:01,530
My pleasure, Son.

103
00:07:01,530 --> 00:07:04,530
Oh, and, Robbie ...

104
00:07:04,530 --> 00:07:05,530
Yes?

105
00:07:05,530 --> 00:07:08,530
You'll probably want the family car

106
00:07:08,530 --> 00:07:11,530
so you can drive her home after the party.

107
00:07:11,530 --> 00:07:12,530
Could I?

108
00:07:12,530 --> 00:07:19,330
If you drive carefully.

109
00:07:19,330 --> 00:07:22,530
I will. Thanks, Dad.

110
00:07:22,530 --> 00:07:24,530
My pleasure.

111
00:07:24,530 --> 00:07:26,530
You're OK, Dad.

112
00:07:26,530 --> 00:07:29,530
You're not so bad yourself, Son.
